.TITLE "ip"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manages network interfaces, routing, and tunnels. It is the modern replacement for the legacy __ifconfig__ command and provides more powerful control over the Linux networking stack.

.DIV "TLDR"
**ip address**
Displays all network interfaces and their assigned IP addresses.
> __address__ subcommand

**ip link set interface up**
Activates a specific network interface.
> __link set__ subcommand | __interface__ name (e.g., eth0) | __up__ state

**ip link set interface down**
Deactivates a specific network interface.
> __link set__ subcommand | __interface__ name | __down__ state

**ip route**
Displays the current IP routing table for the system.
> __route__ subcommand

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __ip__ command is part of the __iproute2__ package. It is highly recommended to use __ip__ instead of __ifconfig__, as it provides a more consistent interface and supports advanced networking features like policy routing.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:ping** **cli:netstat** **cli:ss**

